# Every text file is checked out with LF line endings on every system, Windows included.
# The bundled chart templates, the Field Station sample and the test fixtures are compiled
# in and compared byte for byte, so a CRLF checkout (Git for Windows' default) would change
# what the Windows build ships and fail those tests (found by the first nightly build).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Kept byte for byte, never converted: spreadsheets (one test file is plain text with CRLF
# on purpose, to be refused as "not a zip").
*.xlsx binary
